# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Recovery's UI library (overlay/recovery) gives eth0 the SLiRP address
# 10.0.2.15/24 itself, so that the host's forward to that address reaches adbd:
# SIOCSIFADDR (0x8916) and SIOCSIFNETMASK (0x891c) on a UDP socket. init cannot
# run a tool for it from recovery's domain, and the stock policy gives that
# domain no UDP socket, so socket() failed with EACCES, recovery logged "Failed
# to open socket: Permission denied", and eth0 kept no IPv4 address. The domain
# holds CAP_NET_ADMIN already; this grants the socket and those two ioctls and
# nothing else. Only recovery runs in this domain, so the rules are inert in
# the system's policy, like Cuttlefish's own recovery rules.
allow recovery self:udp_socket { create ioctl };
allowxperm recovery self:udp_socket ioctl { 0x8916 0x891c };
